From cef21d1ee4f0e5b6befdbff15712aea04382c0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:38:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] Import concurrency in Rules, one lane per import job

Rules::concurrency (default 16, the old CONCURRENCY constant) sets the requests
an import keeps in flight, so a caller can open a stream's import wider.

Each import Job takes its own Lane for its STAT and BODY requests (fork
0156be60's queue part), so one job never pipelines behind another job's stalled
reply. body_in_lane and body_unremembered take a lane and a BodyExpectation, so
the first-part checks keep working inside the lane.
